# Building Atrinik client

Install Python 3.11 or newer, CMake 3.21 or newer, Ninja, a C17 compiler,
SDL >= 3.4, SDL3_image/SDL3_ttf >= 3.2, SDL3_mixer >= 3.2.4,
OpenSSL >= 3.5, and LibXml2. Client builds also need
DXC and SPIRV-Cross to compile the authoritative HLSL source. Install those
tools system-wide or prepare the pinned versions once, then build:

```sh
python3 tools/dependencies.py sync
python3 tools/prepare_gpu_shader_toolchain.py \
  --cache build/gpu-shader-downloads \
  --output build/gpu-shader-toolchain
cmake --preset linux-debug
cmake --build --preset linux-debug
ctest --preset linux-debug
```

Running the production client requires a hardware GPU exposed through SDL_GPU
using Vulkan, Direct3D 12, or Metal, with RGBA8 and R32_UINT render-target
support and a D32_FLOAT depth attachment. Software and CPU-emulated drivers are suitable only for test
conformance and are not a supported runtime fallback. If device, format,
shader, or swapchain initialization fails, the client reports the backend and
driver diagnostics and exits without entering play.

Generated DXIL, SPIR-V, and MSL are embedded at build time and never compiled
on the player's machine. `shaders/SHA256SUMS` locks the expected output cohort;
an intentional `shaders/map.hlsl` change must regenerate and review that small
manifest. CI and release packaging reuse one validated cohort through the
`ATRINIK_GPU_SHADER_DIRECTORY` CMake cache variable.

Release builds use the same configure-time interface as the integrated and
server builds: `-DATRINIK_PACKAGE_VERSION=MAJOR.MINOR.PATCH`. Without it,
CMake uses the packaged `VERSION` file, an exact release tag, or the shared
deterministic developer fallback, in that order. The resolved version and
compiler/platform benchmark provenance are embedded in the executable.

The Classic protocol must be available from the sibling `protocol/` tree, the
packaged `dependencies/protocol` tree, or CMake's
`FETCHCONTENT_SOURCE_DIR_ATRINIK_PROTOCOL` override. This keeps the client and
its evolving wire contract on the same repository revision.

The matching Classic libatrinik source must also come from the sibling
`libatrinik/` tree, packaged `dependencies/libatrinik` tree, or
`FETCHCONTENT_SOURCE_DIR_LIBATRINIK` override. Use protocol and library sources
from the same reviewed Classic revision. Bare component builds fail at configure
when these sources are missing; they do not download a historical standalone
library release. Scoped source archives already include both matching trees.
A parent SDK project may provide the compatible `Atrinik::Core` target instead;
its package version must retain the actual unified Classic version.

The client uses direct module headers and has no client precompiled-header
mode. Every source and test therefore exercises the same conventional include
graph. See `../docs/BUILD_ACCELERATION.md` for the server PCH benchmark
procedure and invalidation tradeoffs.

Discord Rich Presence is optional. A build without an Application ID remains
fully functional and opens no Discord IPC endpoint. For an installed/package
build, pass a one-line numeric file with
`-DATRINIK_DISCORD_APPLICATION_ID_FILE=/absolute/path/to/file`; CMake validates
and installs it as `data/discord-application-id` without compiling the value
into `atrinik`. Local source runs may instead set the public, non-secret
`ATRINIK_DISCORD_APPLICATION_ID` environment variable or create the ignored
`data/discord-application-id` file. Never supply a Discord Client Secret,
OAuth token, bot token, authorization code, or user credential.

Linux x86_64 releases provide
`atrinik-classic-client-VERSION-linux-x86_64.AppImage`. Verify the downloaded
file against `SHA256SUMS`, make it executable with `chmod +x`, and run it directly.
The baseline is Ubuntu 24.04 or newer x86_64 with glibc >= 2.39. The AppImage
bundles SDL >= 3.4 and the other application libraries; no APT SDL installation
is required. The host still supplies the kernel, hardware GPU drivers, Vulkan
loader, and desktop/audio services. Alpine/musl and ARM are outside this contract.
If FUSE mounting is unavailable, pass `--appimage-extract-and-run`; the pinned
static-FUSE type-2 runtime does not require host libfuse2. Replace the downloaded
file to upgrade; user data remains in `.atrinik/<major>.x/`, including when
`ATRINIK_CONFIG_DIR` selects an isolated configuration base. There is no automatic
updater or store integration. See `../docs/RELEASING.md` for packaging and
separate desktop qualification. Source-build dependency requirements above are
unchanged.

Windows portable packages install the checked-in Mozilla-derived `ca-bundle.crt`.
The client release helper explicitly selects that source bundle; standalone CMake
builds may still set `ATRINIK_CA_BUNDLE` deliberately. When the selected Windows
runtime DLLs include c-ares, packaging also requires its complete license at
`ATRINIK_WINDOWS_RUNTIME_DIR/../share/licenses/c-ares/LICENSE.md`, or the explicit
`ATRINIK_WINDOWS_CARES_LICENSE` override, and installs it as `c-ares-LICENSE.md`
beside the DLLs. Toolchains without a c-ares DLL do not require that notice.
